; The reader's floats (sys/io/read.lisp, XR-READ-FLONUM): a decimal literal is
; read as the correctly rounded IEEE single, to nearest, ties to even; past the
; largest single it is an infinity, and below the smallest normal single it
; underflows as arithmetic does (FLOATING-EXPONENT-UNDERFLOW, or 0.0 under
; ZUNDERFLOW; no subnormal is made), read from a string so that the error is
; the case's.  Each case gives the single's bits, %POINTER of the float, with the
; sign apart.  The reader rounded twice (12 digits made a float, then a power
; of ten scaled it), and was a unit in the last place off for some literals:
; 1.570796326 was #x3FC90FDA.  The first three cases are controls, exact
; either way.  Run with --compile --files sys/io/read.lisp.
